WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.880
A dozen gold bars were seized in a Collingwood OPP probe that charged two people. This is Collingwood Weekly, episode 7. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. I don't live in Collingwood. After that file, wasaga's beach drive closure, grey county's winter shelter rooms, and roads and weather ahead. Collingwood OPP, Barry Today Reports, spent months on a trafficking investigation with search warrants for houses in Collingwood, in Midland and in other places across Ontario.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:34.280
The seizure list also takes in guns, two crossbows, 29 cell phones, other weapons, drugs

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:34.960
and cash.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.920
Kowortha 411 says the two people charged are Peterborough residents.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.020
Barry 360 called it a massive seizure in a probe this detachment led.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.860
They are accused that is not a finding of guilt.

00:00:47.051 --> 00:00:50.531
Beach Drive in Wessaga Beach is still shut from Spruce Street to Third Street.

00:00:50.891 --> 00:00:51.611
The town says.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:56.411
Beach Area 1 can still be reached from the Geneta Street Lot, the Spruce Lot, the Third

00:00:56.411 --> 00:01:00.811
Street Laught off 2nd or 3rd, the 4th Street Laught, and the Nancy Laught on Mosley.

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:05.851
The Playland Lots crossing in Beach Path are closed for the year, though parking, washrooms,

00:01:06.051 --> 00:01:08.151
and the municipal food truck area stay open.

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:13.491
The town points people who need a flatter route to a wide path on 3rd, a mobility mat, and

00:01:13.491 --> 00:01:15.391
a path into the municipal picnic area.

00:01:15.851 --> 00:01:21.351
The rebuild lifts the road about 5 feet, roughly 1.5 meters, after repeated flooding, with

00:01:21.351 --> 00:01:23.911
the province putting in about 10.9 million dollars.

00:01:23.911 --> 00:01:29.151
That same update said Mosley Street roundabout repairs will start and disrupt traffic, while

00:01:29.151 --> 00:01:33.951
pavers, curb, sidewalk, grading, and electrical work keep going on beach drive.

00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:38.377
G-bay girls handed $44,000 to Georgian Bay Charities.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:40.457
CTV News reported this week.

00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:46.737
A gala brought in over $345,000 for Bright Shores Meferred Hospital, Collingwood Today reported.

00:01:47.437 --> 00:01:50.697
Collingwood has put in a veterans' crosswalk to honor service and sacrifice.

00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:52.317
CTV News reported.

00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:57.757
The same network called it an interactive reminder of that sacrifice, and Simco.com framed

00:01:57.757 --> 00:02:00.157
the crossing as ready and time for Remembrance Day.

00:02:00.597 --> 00:02:05.417
A coroner's inquest is now called in the death of Miford resident Tanya Hornjackov, Midland

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:06.157
today reported.

00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:10.457
She died in hospital after a transfer from the Central North Correctional Center four

00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:14.017
years ago, and the report ties the case to the Penitang Superjail.

00:02:15.026 --> 00:02:19.606
Gray County, at the council table in the form of its winter notice, says plows, salt

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:24.826
domes and operators are ready, and it wants winter tires plus a shovel, blanket, booster

00:02:24.826 --> 00:02:26.466
cables, and a flashlight in the car.

00:02:27.106 --> 00:02:31.766
Plows run between 25 and 60 kilometers an hour, and the county never recommends passing

00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:32.026
one.

00:02:32.526 --> 00:02:37.666
On Grey Road 14 in Southgate last January, Whiteout conditions contributed to a five vehicle

00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:39.866
crash that sent a plow operator to hospital.

00:02:40.306 --> 00:02:44.606
Don't drive around a barricade, pull into a lot or a driveway instead of stopping on the

00:02:44.606 --> 00:02:48.726
road, and conditions a map and cameras sit at roads.gray.ca.

00:02:49.246 --> 00:02:53.306
A stranded vehicle can be reported on the county line, and anyone in danger should call

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.066
9-1-1.

00:02:54.506 --> 00:03:00.466
Plow name voting closes today, Friday, November 6th, at connectgray.ca, and it needs a registered

00:03:00.466 --> 00:03:00.846
account.

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.446
More than 650 suggestions came in.

00:03:03.906 --> 00:03:09.106
The short list includes Sled Zeppelin, Darth Blader, Frostodamus, and Lady Penelope

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:10.946
Plowington, Duchess of Drift.

00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:12.746
Winners are due November 10th.

00:03:12.746 --> 00:03:17.120
The Simco County District School Board has a policy consultation open,

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.800
Barry Today reported, and the current period runs until December 4.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.720
Waisaga Beach scheduled Schunertown Bridge expansion joint seal work to start November 2,

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:26.880
weather permitting.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.660
Crews remove the old seals, clean the joints and install new ones,

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.020
keeping through traffic with only short lane cuts,

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.980
and the town expects one to two weeks depending on weather.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.980
The named contacts are Steve M.B. at Aynley Group,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.680
and Mike Penicivero, the town's manager of engineering services.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:48.254
Gray County is switching its short-term shelter program to winter operations with an average

00:03:48.254 --> 00:03:52.534
of 47 motel rooms a night up from 44 in last year's winter figure.

00:03:53.074 --> 00:03:57.654
The rooms include a county-owned former motel and Owen Sound and other motels in the county.

00:03:58.294 --> 00:04:02.914
Bayshore broadcasting said that Owen Sound Building on 9th Avenue East was converted

00:04:02.914 --> 00:04:04.754
from a motel into short-term housing.

00:04:05.174 --> 00:04:10.294
The higher capacity usually runs from November 1 to March 31 and can shift with the weather.

00:04:10.294 --> 00:04:17.334
Council in January 2024 told staff to finish buying the diamond motor in at 713 9th Avenue

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.554
East for $3.05 million.

00:04:20.314 --> 00:04:25.694
A room then cost about $120 a night, and the purchase was projected to cut that to 52.

00:04:26.354 --> 00:04:35.194
In 2025, the program provided 9,324 nights, supported 366 adults and 59 youth age 16 and younger,

00:04:35.554 --> 00:04:37.434
and the average day was 25 days.

00:04:38.414 --> 00:04:42.034
126 households moved into self-contained places when their stay ended.

00:04:42.394 --> 00:04:48.274
The Owen Sound Current reported in January that 155 households in Grey County were recorded

00:04:48.274 --> 00:04:52.534
as actively homeless at the end of 2025, a slight drop from the year before.

00:04:53.134 --> 00:04:57.594
Anne-Marie Shaw, the county's director of community services, said Grey County winters

00:04:57.594 --> 00:05:01.974
can be harsh, especially for those without a safe place to stay, and that the program

00:05:01.974 --> 00:05:06.574
provides an important option for individuals and families who need somewhere safe, warm

00:05:06.574 --> 00:05:07.654
and welcoming to turn.

00:05:08.154 --> 00:05:10.594
Housing case coordinators connect people with services,

00:05:11.054 --> 00:05:12.754
housing plans, and permanent housing.

00:05:13.154 --> 00:05:14.974
The county also backs safe and sound

00:05:14.974 --> 00:05:16.474
Greybruse drop-in programming

00:05:16.474 --> 00:05:18.714
and a new overnight shelter in Owen Sound.

00:05:19.354 --> 00:05:22.514
County money and community donations fund those overnight hours,

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.514
and Owen Sound Council approved up to $30,000

00:05:25.514 --> 00:05:27.574
in city grants toward that shelter in July.

00:05:28.134 --> 00:05:30.214
The Shelter Program has a published phone line

00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:33.814
and the email STSPAT gray.ca.

00:05:33.814 --> 00:05:39.794
Awasaga Beach resident took home more than $392,000 in Royal Victoria Regional Health

00:05:39.794 --> 00:05:41.414
